{"name":"White Pudding","hex":"#f6e8df","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white pudding","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A meat dish, made from minced pork and oats cooked in a sausage skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white_pudding"}],"entries":[{"title":"White pudding","blocks":[{"text":"White pudding, oatmeal pudding or mealy pudding is a meat dish in Great Britain and Ireland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Irish_black_and_white_pudding_slices.JPG/330px-Irish_black_and_white_pudding_slices.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_pudding","wikidata":"Q1332967"},{"title":"Pudding","blocks":[{"text":"Pudding is a food which can either be a dessert or a savoury dish. In the United States, pudding means a sweet, milk-based dessert similar in consistency to egg-based custards, instant custards or a mousse, often commercially set using cornstarch, gelatin or similar coagulating agent. These puddings are known in some Commonwealth countries as custards if they are egg-thickened, as blancmange if starch-thickened, and as jelly if gelatin-based. Pudding in America may also refer to other dishes such as bread pudding and rice pudding, although typically these names derive from their origin as British dishes. The modern American meaning of pudding as dessert has evolved from the original almost exclusive use of the term to describe savoury dishes, specifically those created using a process similar to that used for sausages, in which meat and other ingredients in mostly liquid form are encased and then steamed or boiled to set the contents."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Blanc-manger_on_glass_platter%2C_full_view.jpg/330px-Blanc-manger_on_glass_platter%2C_full_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pudding","wikidata":"Q9053"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Haggis_with_a_CC_license.jpg/500px-Haggis_with_a_CC_license.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Haggis_with_a_CC_license.jpg/500px-Haggis_with_a_CC_license.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Haggis, a savoury pudding","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHaggis_with_a_CC_license.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Pudding_With_Raspberries_and_Whipped_Cream.jpg/500px-Pudding_With_Raspberries_and_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Pudding_With_Raspberries_and_Whipped_Cream.jpg/1280px-Pudding_With_Raspberries_and_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Pudding_With_Raspberries_and_Whipped_Cream.jpg/500px-Pudding_With_Raspberries_and_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pudding of the dessert type may be served with toppings such as fresh fruit and whipped cream.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APudding_With_Raspberries_and_Whipped_Cream.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Kheer.jpg/500px-Kheer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Kheer.jpg/1280px-Kheer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Kheer.jpg/500px-Kheer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kheer, from India, here made with rice","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKheer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Christmas_pudding.JPG/330px-Christmas_pudding.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Christmas_pudding.JPG/330px-Christmas_pudding.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Christmas pudding","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChristmas_pudding.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/79/Chocolate_pudding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/79/Chocolate_pudding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Instant dessert pudding","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChocolate_pudding.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Canonization_2014-The_Canonization_of_Saint_John_XXIII_and_Saint_John_Paul_II_%2814037015405%29.jpg/500px-Canonization_2014-The_Canonization_of_Saint_John_XXIII_and_Saint_John_Paul_II_%2814037015405%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, htt